# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_http_security_headers.py" "CORE HTTP SECURITY HEADERS: PASS" "core http security headers" "core HTTP boundary (public status, operator probes, webhook rejects, and webhook accepts inherit the JSON/API-only security-header baseline; repository delete/deselection stays persist-before-202 under the ordinary-event durable-inbox kill switch; and /healthz, /readyz, plus coarse /statusz fail closed when the dedicated durable-owner heartbeat daemon is dead/stale even though event worker threads remain alive, while legacy/no-store seams preserve worker-only health)" "core HTTP security + lease-liveness composition (locks the public-launch header baseline, keeps offboarding delivery-keyed, and prevents probes from reporting green after the cross-instance lease-authority heartbeat stops)" 24
